**Issue**: #423
**Date**: 2026-09-23
**Status**: Approved
**Author**: NMG

Feature: Historical smoke failures do not own changed verification attempts

  @AC1 @AC4
  Scenario: A changed head and queue starts a fresh owned smoke attempt
    Given plugin issue #418 retains an old failed #133 artifact and clone
    And the new #135 request has a different exact identity and no matching recovery-store owner
    When registered smoke verification starts
    Then it preserves old evidence and clones a fresh smoke workspace for #135
    And it records a new #135 baseline before dispatching the owned controller
    And only a new exact-head merged implementation PR and closed #135 can pass

  @AC1
  Scenario: A changed queue alone is historical
    Given an internally attributable old smoke queue differs from the current explicit queue
    When legacy recovery is inspected without a current store owner
    Then old nested work is not replayed or deleted
    And the current queue follows fresh clone and baseline checks

  @AC2
  Scenario: Matching but unsafe recovery cannot dispatch twice
    Given an old artifact belongs to the exact current identity and queue
    And its failure evidence is malformed, ambiguous, nonterminal or unproved
    When legacy recovery is inspected
    Then the provider fails with legacy recovery evidence invalid
    And no clone or controller dispatch occurs

  @AC3
  Scenario: Matching valid failed delivery resumes once
    Given an exact-identity failed delivery has valid legacy recovery proof
    When the provider resumes its retained invocation
    Then it uses bounded recovery without a second nested dispatch
